INT. DUBBING STUDIO BOOTH - NIGHT

A padded booth the size of a closet. Acoustic foam in grey waves. A microphone on a boom arm. A music stand holding a script, pages curling. A small red light on the wall, dark for now.

Beyond a thick glass pane, an empty control room. A mixing desk glows green. No one sits behind it.

IRENKA VESELY, 78, perches on a stool, headphones around her neck, lace collar buttoned to the chin. Silver hair pinned back. Heavy rings on both hands. She has the kind of face that was once on posters.

A monitor on the wall shows a silent black-and-white clip: a young woman's face, laughing.

Irenka watches it. She does not laugh.

She reaches over. Presses a button on a small tape deck beside the stand. It clicks.

IRENKA (V.O.)
(tape, thirty years younger, brisk)
"I never said I loved you. I said I would stay."

Irenka listens. Nods slowly. Presses stop.

IRENKA
Too quick.

She rewinds the tape. Plays it again.

IRENKA (V.O.)
(tape)
"I never said I loved you. I said I would stay."

IRENKA
Still too quick.

She switches off the deck. Slips the headphones on. Leans toward the microphone. The red light glows on.

IRENKA (CONT'D)
(reading)
"I never said I loved you."

Her voice cracks. She stops. Clears her throat. Looks up at the monitor. The young face laughs again.

IRENKA (CONT'D)
(to herself)
She was never in a hurry.

She tries again.

IRENKA (CONT'D)
"I never said I loved you. I said --"

She stops. Pulls the headphones down. Sits in the silence for a long moment.

IRENKA (CONT'D)
(to the glass)
You always did make me say it twice.

No answer. The green desk glows.

She reaches for the deck again. Presses a different button. A second tape hisses.

IRENKA (V.O.)
(tape, much younger, laughing)
"Pavel, put that down. We are rolling."

A man's cough on the tape, nothing more, then the clink of a glass. She smiles. The smile slips.

IRENKA (V.O.) (CONT'D)
(tape)
"Take one. Irenka Vesely. 'The Quiet Hour.'"

The tape hisses. Ends. She sits with the deck, hands folded around it, as if keeping it warm.

IRENKA
(whispering)
Take one.

She sets the deck on the floor. Stands. Her knees crack. She grips the mic stand.

She puts on the headphones. Faces the microphone. Straightens her spine as if a director stood behind her.

IRENKA (CONT'D)
(to the room)
Ready, everyone?

Nobody answers. She smiles, tight and brave.

IRENKA (CONT'D)
Ready when you are.

The red light blinks on. She takes a long breath. Eyes on the monitor. On the young face. On the young smile.

IRENKA (CONT'D)
(slow, warm, barely a whisper)
"I never said I loved you."

A beat. The young face on the monitor turns toward an unseen man and smiles.

IRENKA (CONT'D)
"I said I would stay."

The red light blinks off. Silence.

She doesn't move. Her hands are steady. Her shoulders are not.

IRENKA (CONT'D)
(a whisper)
It took me sixty years.

The monitor fades to black. She stays, listening to the room.

She gathers her handbag, her cardigan, her gloves. At the door she pauses. Looks back at the empty control room, the glowing desk.

IRENKA (CONT'D)
(to the booth)
I'll be here tomorrow.

She opens the door. Light from the corridor spills over her shoulders. She steps out, leaving the booth dark.

The tape deck, at her feet, clicks on by itself.

IRENKA (V.O.)
(tape, faint)
"Take two."
